# Same config as zernie/vigiles: Prettier defaults, no config file. This list names
# only what a tool writes or what is kept as exact bytes; everything else is formatted.

# Every skills/*/SKILL.md is COMPILED from its SKILL.md.spec.ts by `vigiles compile`,
# which owns the exact bytes and stamps an integrity hash over them. Prettier would
# re-escape markdown and desync the hash, so the two gates would fight forever.
# The spec (SKILL.md.spec.ts) IS formatted.
skills/*/SKILL.md

# Test inputs: the rules under test read these bytes, and some are judged against a
# recorded baseline. Reflowing a fixture changes what the test measures. The fixture
# CODE (harnesses, the baseline reader) is formatted.
fixtures/**
!fixtures/**/
!fixtures/**/*.mjs

# Raw runs kept exactly as they ran — the evidence behind a written number. Their
# bytes are the record (same class as vigiles' docs/design/probes/).
docs/prior-art/repro/
skills/paper-pipeline/repro/
skills/paper-pipeline/references/occupancy-2026-08-06-probe/
